{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310659,"nonce":"DdBT4xdH3fkvbIKY9aODnL/fROk=","title":"FIXED — `Null\u003cT\u003e + Int` and `Null\u003cT\u003e + Null\u003cT\u003e` arithmetic produced garbage/SIGBUS. Binop lowering ignored boxed DynamicValue* shape; also ...","message":"`debug_channel` printed `5 / \u003cgarbage\u003e / done` instead of `5 / 100 / done`. Distilled to a non-channel repro:\n\n```haxe\nvar a:Null\u003cInt\u003e = 42;\nvar b:Null\u003cInt\u003e = 7;\nvar s = a + b;   // SIGBUS / garbage\n```\n\n\nTwo-layer bug in [hir_to_mir.rs](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs):\n\n1. **Binop lowering didn't unbox Null operands** — the arithmetic binop path lowered each operand via `lower_expression` and then called `build_binop(Add, lhs_reg, rhs_reg)` directly. For `Null\u003cInt\u003e` operands, `convert_type(Optional{Int})` returns `Ptr(U8)` (boxed DynamicValue*), so the binop ran on raw pointer values.\n\n2. **`maybe_unbox_optional` missed the (I64, I64) case** — `Channel\u003cT\u003e.tryReceive()` returns `Null\u003cT\u003e` where T is a TypeParameter. After generic instantiation T's MIR type is `I64` (per `convert_type` for TypeParameter). The existing `maybe_unbox_optional` covered (I32, I32), (F64, F64), (Bool, Bool) but not (I64, I64), so even when called the unbox silently bailed via `_ =\u003e None`.\n\n\nIn the arithmetic binop arm of `lower_expression_inner`:\n\n```rust\nif matches!(op, HirBinaryOp::Add | Sub | Mul | Div | Mod) {\n    if self.is_optional_primitive(lhs.ty) {\n        if let Some(inner) = self.optional_inner_type(lhs.ty) {\n            if let Some(unboxed) = self.maybe_unbox_optional(lhs_reg, lhs.ty, inner) {\n                lhs_reg = unboxed;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // ... same for rhs\n}\n```\n\nDrive off each operand's own inner primitive type — not `expr.ty`, which the typechecker may leave as `Null\u003cInt\u003e` after unifying mixed branches.\n\nAdd `(IrType::I64, IrType::I64) =\u003e haxe_unbox_int_ptr` arm to `maybe_unbox_optional`.\n\nAdd a small `optional_inner_type(TypeId) -\u003e Option\u003cTypeId\u003e` helper next to `is_optional_primitive`.\n\n\nWhen the MIR register type for an operand differs from what convert_type(operand.ty) suggests (because the value carries a boxed/wrapper shape that downstream consumers don't know about), the lowering must reconcile shapes BEFORE calling build_binop / build_cmp / build_cast. The existing `maybe_unbox_optional`, `maybe_box_for_optional`, and `maybe_abstract_from_convert` helpers are the canonical places — extend them rather than hand-rolling new logic.\n\nWhenever extending those helpers for a new primitive type lowering, remember TypeParameter erasure paths: `TypeParameter` converts to `I64` regardless of constraint, so any helper that switches on `inner_ir` must explicitly include the I64 arm or generic instantiations will silently bypass it.\n\nVerification: full suite stable at 128/128 across 3 consecutive runs after fix. `debug_channel` prints `5 / 100 / done`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_null_arith_no_unbox` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}